Supplementary Technical Documentation
Driving Simulator Assessment and Training Scenarios
This document provides a technical description of the standardized driving simulator scenarios used during the baseline assessment (Scenario 1 and 2) and intervention phases (Scenarios 3–7) of the Drive-Fun study. All scenarios were provided by the commercially available 3D-Fahrschule simulator and were not modified by the research team.

Scenario 1 – Baseline Assessment Drive 1
Scenario Characteristics
Basic urban driving scenario.
Driving Environment
Standardized urban driving environment.
Approximate Duration
Approximately 4 minutes (duration varied slightly according to each participant's driving speed and performance).
Driving Events
•	6 traffic lights
•	3 yield signs
•	3 pedestrian crossings
•	4 right turns
•	4 opportunities to use turn signals
Primary Driving Objectives
•	Baseline assessment of fundamental driving performance.
•	Compliance with traffic signs and traffic lights.
•	Safe lane keeping and right turns.
•	Maintaining an appropriate urban driving speed.
Typical Driving Challenges
•	Basic intersections.
•	Traffic light compliance.
•	Yield signs.
•	Initial signaling opportunities.
Automatically Recorded Performance Measures
•	Failure to yield
•	Traffic light violations
•	Speeding
•	Pedestrian collisions
•	Wrong turns
•	Incorrect signaling
